1
00:00:01,167 --> 00:00:03,800
<i>Mom, I still don't know
how this happened to you.</i>

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:05,833
<i> I got this inside.</i>

3
00:00:05,967 --> 00:00:07,033
<i> Looks like a camera.</i>

4
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:08,867
<i>Are you sure that's the Korean
we're looking for?</i>

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,533
<i>- Yes, Sir.
- Who is he talking to?</i>

6
00:00:10,667 --> 00:00:12,167
<i> Dad, that's Theresa.</i>

7
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:14,067
<i>She's the woman Jin Ho
wants to capture.</i>

8
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,500
<i>I also want to meet the man
you brought into this group.</i>

9
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:17,633
<i> Stop this nonsense!</i>

10
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:19,300
<i>Is this really how you are
when I'm not here?</i>

11
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:21,500
<i>Is this how you handle
this place?</i>

12
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:23,767
<i>Andrew is going through
something heavy right now.</i>

13
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:24,833
<i> Call him.</i>

14
00:00:24,967 --> 00:00:25,967
<i> Where's Andrew?</i>

15
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,900
<i>He's preparing things
to bring to the hospital</i>

16
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:29,400
<i> for Mommy Rebecca.</i>

17
00:00:29,533 --> 00:00:30,567
<i> "Mommy?"</i>

18
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,567
<i>I guess I should get used
to calling her that</i>

19
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,567
<i>since things are getting better
between me and Andrew.</i>

20
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,300
<i> [OBB]</i>

21
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:58,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

22
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:02,533
I guess you're back together.

23
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:04,100
That's good.

24
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:05,667
Congratulations to you.

25
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:07,767
Joey...

26
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:10,633
<i> Thanks for being happy for us.</i>

27
00:01:10,767 --> 00:01:11,900
We're not yet official

28
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:15,767
but we both know that's where
it's heading, right?

29
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,267
<i> You know, Joey...</i>

30
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:20,833
I wish you'd find the person
meant for you too.

31
00:01:20,967 --> 00:01:22,133
<i>You know what?
I can help you with that.</i>

32
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:24,300
I can introduce you
to some of my friends,

33
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:26,333
<i> maybe you'll like one of them.</i>

34
00:01:26,467 --> 00:01:28,367
I'm not looking for a partner.

35
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,033
Are you sure?

36
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:33,633
Because I just want you
to be happy,

37
00:01:33,767 --> 00:01:35,133
Just like us.

38
00:01:35,267 --> 00:01:37,033
Just like me and Andrew.

39
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,567
<i>Anyway, if you change your mind</i>

40
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,633
or you need help,

41
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:46,767
I'll set you up, just tell me.
Okay, I have to go,

42
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:48,400
Andrew and I have something
to do.

43
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:49,967
Bye!

44
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:56,300
You're here.

45
00:01:56,967 --> 00:01:58,500
- Andrew!
- We're about to leave.

46
00:01:58,633 --> 00:02:00,300
Yes, let's go.

47
00:02:03,233 --> 00:02:05,067
Why do you have my phone?

48
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:06,767 --> 00:02:08,500
Nothing, I just wanted
to give it to you.

50
00:02:08,633 --> 00:02:09,633
You might forget it.

51
00:02:09,767 --> 00:02:11,133
Here.

52
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:15,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:15,467 --> 00:02:16,433
Excuse me.

54
00:02:16,567 --> 00:02:17,867
Okay.

55
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

56
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,600
<i> Gosh, so arrogant!</i>

57
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:34,267
[PHONE CHIMES]

58
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:38,400
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:02:45,033 --> 00:02:46,100
Jin Ho?

60
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:49,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

61
00:03:00,367 --> 00:03:04,567
[LIGHT AMBIENT MUSIC PLAYING]

62
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:17,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:03:26,533 --> 00:03:30,000
Go ahead and enjoy your coffee

64
00:03:30,133 --> 00:03:32,267
because that'll be your last.

65
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,333
You're doomed.

66
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:40,367
[LIGHT AMBIENT MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:03:51,967 --> 00:03:53,267
Jin Ho.

68
00:03:55,233 --> 00:03:56,867
Joey...

69
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,833
You got me there.

70
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:00,433
Have a seat first.

71
00:04:00,567 --> 00:04:04,700
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:08,200
What happened to you?

73
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:09,733
Did you get into a fight?

74
00:04:09,867 --> 00:04:11,767
Who did you fight?

75
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:17,233
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:18,933
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

77
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:22,567
Got you.

78
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:25,267
<i>So, you're quite
the ladies' man.</i>

79
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:28,967
Let's see if Lisa will help you

80
00:04:29,133 --> 00:04:31,567
when she finds out
you're two-timing her.

81
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:35,733
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

82
00:04:36,967 --> 00:04:38,133
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]
It's nothing.

83
00:04:38,267 --> 00:04:40,767
It's just work hazard.

84
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,700
That's why I wanted to see you.

85
00:04:43,833 --> 00:04:46,767
I need to forget work
for a while.

86
00:04:48,367 --> 00:04:50,200
Okay.

87
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,733
I thought you're going
to invite the others.

88
00:04:53,633 --> 00:04:54,767
- Others?
- Yes.

89
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,433
Is Peter still
at the boarding house?

90
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:58,767
No...

91
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:02,200
Peter went to his province.

92
00:05:02,367 --> 00:05:04,200
What about Andrew?

93
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:07,467
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,567
He's with his girlfriend.

95
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:12,700
He has a girlfriend, really?

96
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,700
I mean...

97
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:19,967
All this time, I thought the
two of you will end up together.

98
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,533
No, never!

99
00:05:22,867 --> 00:05:24,233
Uncle, wait!

100
00:05:24,367 --> 00:05:25,567
Don't leave yet.

101
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,900
Uncle Andrew, we need your help.

102
00:05:28,033 --> 00:05:30,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,333
Okay, what is this?

104
00:05:35,133 --> 00:05:36,567
I can't fix this.

105
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:40,600
Can you fix this?

106
00:05:40,733 --> 00:05:42,433
Yes, Sir.

107
00:05:43,633 --> 00:05:45,700
Thank you,
and if you can't fix it,

108
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:47,600
please tell my sister,

109
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:49,100
maybe she can have it fixed.

110
00:05:49,233 --> 00:05:52,300
- Yes, Sir.
- Okay, problem solved.

111
00:05:52,433 --> 00:05:54,033
- Anyway...
- And, Uncle...

112
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,700
we need your help too.

113
00:05:57,967 --> 00:05:59,767
As just as much
as I wanna help you,

114
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:01,800
I really can't right now

115
00:06:01,933 --> 00:06:04,533
because grandmother is alone
at the hospital.

116
00:06:04,667 --> 00:06:05,533
I'm sorry.

117
00:06:05,667 --> 00:06:08,100
But I promise when I return,

118
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:09,667
I'll help you.

119
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,567
Is that okay?

120
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:12,933
Okay, Uncle Andrew. Promise?

121
00:06:13,067 --> 00:06:14,067
Promise.

122
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,067
Kiss grandmother for us, please.

123
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,800
I will.

124
00:06:19,933 --> 00:06:21,800
- Anyway, I'll go, okay?
- Okay, take care!

125
00:06:21,933 --> 00:06:23,067
Bye!

126
00:06:25,467 --> 00:06:27,433
I'm really curious
if this still works,

127
00:06:27,567 --> 00:06:30,467
maybe our old videos are here.

128
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:34,100
Maybe daddy can help us?

129
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:36,667
You know what? You stay here.

130
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,300
I'm going to order, my treat.

131
00:06:38,433 --> 00:06:40,267
No, no, I will pay,
I invited you.

132
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,600
No, it's okay, my treat.

133
00:06:41,767 --> 00:06:43,267
Stay there.

134
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,567
[PLEASANT AMBIENT MUSIC PLAYING]

135
00:06:50,667 --> 00:06:52,233
[SPEAKING INAUDIBLY]

136
00:06:52,367 --> 00:06:56,400
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

137
00:06:59,533 --> 00:07:03,533
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:07:11,933 --> 00:07:15,567
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

139
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:31,667
Kang Dae-Hyun.

140
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,400
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:07:35,967 --> 00:07:38,100
He might betray us!

142
00:07:38,233 --> 00:07:42,000
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:07:45,967 --> 00:07:48,267
You are Kang Dae-Hyun, correct?

144
00:07:49,667 --> 00:07:52,433
I just want to ask
a few questions.

145
00:07:55,367 --> 00:07:56,767
[THUDS]

146
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,967
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

147
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:01,067
Stay here! Don't follow us!

148
00:08:03,533 --> 00:08:06,000
I thought
he was with the police.

149
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:10,400
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:18,467
[REVVING]

151
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:22,700
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

152
00:08:24,533 --> 00:08:27,667
[REVVING]

153
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:30,800
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:35,967
[REVVING]

155
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,267
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

156
00:08:42,367 --> 00:08:44,867
[REVVING]

157
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,367
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

158
00:09:02,033 --> 00:09:04,467
[REVVING]

159
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:07,567
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

160
00:09:09,167 --> 00:09:13,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:09:22,367 --> 00:09:23,400
Dad!

162
00:09:24,433 --> 00:09:25,800
Didn't I tell you not to follow?

163
00:09:25,933 --> 00:09:28,133
Dad, I was worried about you.

164
00:09:29,433 --> 00:09:31,133
<i> That Jin Ho is lucky.</i>

165
00:09:31,267 --> 00:09:33,167
He escaped.

166
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:40,267
[REVVING]

167
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,933
Dad, it'd better
if we leave now.

168
00:09:44,567 --> 00:09:46,833
She's right, Miguel,
you two should leave.

169
00:09:46,967 --> 00:09:51,300
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:09:51,433 --> 00:09:52,900
Is that Delgado?

171
00:09:53,033 --> 00:09:55,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,167
Dad, please wear
this again, please.

173
00:10:02,833 --> 00:10:04,733
Get the car,
let's go after him!

174
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:05,900
Don't, Dad!

175
00:10:06,033 --> 00:10:08,467
Someone might recognize you!

176
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,933
Your daughter is right.

177
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:11,767
Go ahead, Miguel,
I'll handle this.

178
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:15,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

179
00:10:24,567 --> 00:10:25,733
Where is he?

180
00:10:25,867 --> 00:10:29,133
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

181
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:41,067
Berdugo...

182
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:44,233
would you know if Delgado's body
has already been released?

183
00:10:44,367 --> 00:10:46,533
What are you saying, Matias?

184
00:10:46,667 --> 00:10:47,900
I don't know.

185
00:10:48,033 --> 00:10:49,267
It feels like I'm being haunted.

186
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:50,700
Haunted?

187
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,133
Matias, I don't have time
for your nonsense.

188
00:10:54,367 --> 00:10:55,667
<i> Sorry, Berdugo.</i>

189
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,600
I think I saw Delgado.

190
00:10:57,733 --> 00:10:59,367
What?

191
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:02,000
Where have you been?

192
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:03,900
I was chased.

193
00:11:04,033 --> 00:11:05,533
Chased?

194
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:08,033
Yes.

195
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,267
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

196
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:13,433
Lisa, I have a problem.

197
00:11:15,033 --> 00:11:17,600
The cops already know
who I really am.

198
00:11:17,733 --> 00:11:19,400
What? How?

199
00:11:19,533 --> 00:11:21,033
I don't know how.

200
00:11:21,167 --> 00:11:22,700
But...

201
00:11:22,833 --> 00:11:26,033
one of them called me
by my real name.

202
00:11:26,167 --> 00:11:27,900
That's why I ran.

203
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:33,700
<i>No, I really think
we're being followed.</i>

204
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:36,233
<i> I think something's wrong.</i>

205
00:11:36,367 --> 00:11:37,767
<i> My gut feels different.</i>

206
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:41,767
I knew it.

207
00:11:41,933 --> 00:11:43,633
Someone was really following us,

208
00:11:43,767 --> 00:11:45,800
and they were after you.

209
00:11:45,933 --> 00:11:47,967
Another problem.

210
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,733
There's no problem, I got away.

211
00:11:49,867 --> 00:11:52,767
- No one followed me here.
- Don't you get it?

212
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:56,233
I can't rely on you
if the police are following you.

213
00:11:56,367 --> 00:11:58,333
I think it's best
if you stay here

214
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:00,233
and lay low for a while.

215
00:12:02,833 --> 00:12:05,367
So you wanna keep me here
like a prisoner?

216
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:06,867
Yes.

217
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,867
I'd rather keep you here
than in prison.

218
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,800
And besides, I could
defend you from Berdugo

219
00:12:12,933 --> 00:12:15,167
if he finds out about this.

220
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:18,967
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

221
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:24,800
Ma'am, I've prepared everything
Ma'am Rebecca needs.

222
00:12:24,933 --> 00:12:25,967
Okay.

223
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,167
Thank you.
I'll bring it myself,

224
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:31,800
and I'll just call you
if I need anything else.

225
00:12:31,933 --> 00:12:33,000
All right.

226
00:12:34,267 --> 00:12:37,400
Sir Tomas, I'll go ahead.

227
00:12:37,533 --> 00:12:38,700
Thank you.

228
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:40,167
Wait, Clarissa.

229
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,933
What is it, Sir?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:45,067
Why, Hon? Do you need something
from Clarissa?

231
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,633
Nothing, I just want
to ask her something.

232
00:12:49,167 --> 00:12:51,733
Has your husband's body
been released?

233
00:12:51,867 --> 00:12:52,900
Has he been buried?

234
00:12:53,033 --> 00:12:53,967
Oh, yes.

235
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:55,500
What the progress?

236
00:12:55,633 --> 00:12:57,433
Not yet.

237
00:12:57,567 --> 00:13:02,300
But Chief told us
that he will help us

238
00:13:02,433 --> 00:13:05,233
until Miguel's body is buried.

239
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:08,400
Maybe it will be released soon.

240
00:13:08,533 --> 00:13:10,300
Well, if you need anything,

241
00:13:10,433 --> 00:13:12,467
just let us know, okay?

242
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,467
We'll be happy to help.

243
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,967
Thank you so much.

244
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,967
- I'll go ahead.
- All right.

245
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:23,200
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

246
00:13:29,633 --> 00:13:32,467
You don't need
to confront Jin Ho.

247
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,633
You're rushing into action

248
00:13:34,767 --> 00:13:37,767
and without the support
of the department.

249
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,833
Sir, it's just that
the opportunity was there.

250
00:13:40,967 --> 00:13:42,533
That's not an excuse.

251
00:13:43,767 --> 00:13:44,767
Sorry, Sir.

252
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:47,200
I should have told you.

253
00:13:47,333 --> 00:13:49,267
Good thing no one saw me,

254
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:52,267
otherwise, my cover of being
dead would be ruined.

255
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:56,133
My bosses are also asking me

256
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:59,667
if Miguel's body
has been released.

257
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,100
I just said it will be
released soon.

258
00:14:02,233 --> 00:14:04,833
Yes, Sir, Is anyone looking
for my body?

259
00:14:04,967 --> 00:14:07,367
Maybe that's what Berdugo
is thinking too.

260
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:10,100
It's not impossible
for the syndicate

261
00:14:10,233 --> 00:14:12,500
to have doubts as long as they
don't see your body

262
00:14:12,633 --> 00:14:14,667
and your burial.

263
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:19,333
Then, let's bury Miguel.

264
00:14:24,467 --> 00:14:26,867
We'll stand by the story
that I'm dead?

265
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,333
Yes.

266
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,100
Thank you.

267
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:36,800
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:40,733
[SWEEPING]

269
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:45,600
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:14:50,167 --> 00:14:52,667
[SWEEPING]

271
00:14:55,033 --> 00:14:56,100
Hey, Peter!

272
00:14:56,233 --> 00:14:58,067
You're up early.

273
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,233
Good morning, Aunt Beng.

274
00:14:59,367 --> 00:15:00,767
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

275
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:05,800
I already put soft drinks
and liquor in the fridge.

276
00:15:05,933 --> 00:15:08,467
And the deliveries
are on their way.

277
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,500
Looks like you woke up
in a good mood, Peter.

278
00:15:10,633 --> 00:15:11,367
Scary.

279
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:12,833
You're crazy!

280
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:17,800
You know, in the few days
I've been here,

281
00:15:17,933 --> 00:15:20,367
I've realized a lot of things.

282
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,800
I've also learned a lot,

283
00:15:21,933 --> 00:15:23,200
especially from you,
Auntie Beng.

284
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:24,933
And from you, Kit.

285
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:27,967
"Gobble, gobble, gobble",
said the turkey.

286
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:32,100
I think I know the point
of scenes like this!

287
00:15:32,233 --> 00:15:35,400
This is exactly how shows go

288
00:15:35,567 --> 00:15:38,167
when someone plans to leave.

289
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:41,667
There, like that, all dressed up
but no shoes yet.

290
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:44,800
Sentimental, thinking about
all the lessons learned

291
00:15:44,933 --> 00:15:48,233
from other people's lives.

292
00:15:48,367 --> 00:15:49,700
You're leaving, Peter?

293
00:15:49,833 --> 00:15:51,400
You're going back to Manila?

294
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:54,967
You know, son...

295
00:15:56,133 --> 00:15:57,433
We're happy that you're here,

296
00:15:57,567 --> 00:16:00,100
and your brother and I are happy

297
00:16:00,233 --> 00:16:02,067
that we helped you
with your problem.

298
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,633
So, that's okay.

299
00:16:03,767 --> 00:16:08,000
Just promise us you'll be
careful in Manila, okay?

300
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,267
Thank you, Auntie Beng.

301
00:16:11,633 --> 00:16:14,067
You, don't forget
what I told you, okay?

302
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:15,233
Of course, Peter.

303
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:16,567
I will be patient.

304
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,267
I will never give up
on the person I love.

305
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,900
I won't be like you.

306
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:24,567
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

307
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:26,200
And not just that.

308
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:27,233
Learn to work hard

309
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,700
and help Auntie Bebeng
in the store

310
00:16:29,833 --> 00:16:31,933
so it would somehow earn.

311
00:16:32,067 --> 00:16:33,100
- Agree!
- Of course, Peter.

312
00:16:33,233 --> 00:16:35,233
I love Auntie Bebeng so much.

313
00:16:35,367 --> 00:16:36,000
Hey.

314
00:16:36,133 --> 00:16:37,533
You're going to kill me.

315
00:16:41,233 --> 00:16:42,567
[SIGHS]

316
00:16:42,733 --> 00:16:44,367
Okay then, come on,

317
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:48,900
let's give this
a power group hug!

318
00:16:49,033 --> 00:16:50,133
[GRUNTING]
Ah, wait, wait!

319
00:16:50,267 --> 00:16:51,367
What is this?

320
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:52,967
Oh my, I'll never get married

321
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:53,900
because of you two.

322
00:16:54,033 --> 00:16:55,500
The two of you are already
too much!

323
00:16:55,633 --> 00:16:56,500
Put me down!

324
00:16:56,633 --> 00:16:57,500
Too much love, Auntie?

325
00:16:57,633 --> 00:16:59,833
No, headache! Down!

326
00:16:59,967 --> 00:17:00,933
[GROANS]

327
00:17:01,067 --> 00:17:02,233
I'll cook breakfast.

328
00:17:02,367 --> 00:17:04,033
Come on, go inside!

329
00:17:04,967 --> 00:17:06,433
Hey, inside!

330
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:08,433
Coming, coming!

331
00:17:08,567 --> 00:17:09,967
Hurry up!

332
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:13,633
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

333
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:23,033
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:17:27,867 --> 00:17:30,300
Condolence, Clarissa and Joey.

335
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,667
Thank you.

336
00:17:33,767 --> 00:17:37,333
It's bad to thank someone
for sympathizing with the dead.

337
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,300
Yes.

338
00:17:42,433 --> 00:17:45,533
Sorry, I just forgot.

339
00:17:45,667 --> 00:17:47,200
Please sit down.

340
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:52,133
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

341
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:55,167
It feels wrong, Mom.

342
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:57,767
Father isn't really dead.

343
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:00,100
Hush!

344
00:18:00,233 --> 00:18:02,500
Someone might hear you.

345
00:18:06,967 --> 00:18:08,233
But, Mom...

346
00:18:09,167 --> 00:18:11,333
I really feel guilty.

347
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:13,667
We're fooling them all.

348
00:18:16,233 --> 00:18:19,800
Once your father completes
his mission,

349
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:22,800
and takes down the syndicate,

350
00:18:23,067 --> 00:18:25,967
I'm sure they'll understand us.

351
00:18:27,033 --> 00:18:30,400
I just hope that time
comes soon

352
00:18:30,533 --> 00:18:32,967
so we won't have to lie
to them anymore.

353
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:37,600
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:18:42,833 --> 00:18:44,167
[PHONE CHIMES]

355
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:53,233
Our friends, Jake and Loy,
offered condolences.

356
00:18:54,433 --> 00:18:55,200
I'm sorry.

357
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:57,267
You got dragged
into my problem too.

358
00:19:03,033 --> 00:19:05,100
If this is the coffee shop,

359
00:19:05,233 --> 00:19:09,300
then where could Berdugo's
drug factory be?

360
00:19:09,433 --> 00:19:11,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

361
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,267
Could it be this?

362
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:17,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

363
00:19:23,167 --> 00:19:24,600
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPS]

364
00:19:24,733 --> 00:19:28,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

365
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:34,600
So, you take charge of Tirada
for now, okay?

366
00:19:34,733 --> 00:19:35,733
Sure, Boss.

367
00:19:35,867 --> 00:19:36,933
We got it covered.

368
00:19:37,067 --> 00:19:38,567
I'm just fixing the script,

369
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:40,933
so we'll have something
to upload.

370
00:19:41,067 --> 00:19:43,167
Then, we'll just bring
the bus here

371
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:44,900
to make it easier for you.

372
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:48,133
Okay, thank you.

373
00:19:48,267 --> 00:19:51,167
Thanks also for visiting mommy.

374
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,933
It wasn't just her we visited.

375
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:55,600
You too, Boss.

376
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:57,100
How are you?

377
00:19:58,033 --> 00:19:59,333
Hoping for the best.

378
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,633
But why are you alone now?

379
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:06,167
Where's your Zoey?

380
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:07,567
[CHUCKLES]

381
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,000
Are you irritated already?
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

382
00:20:09,133 --> 00:20:12,000
Or maybe it's another "Oey"
you want?

383
00:20:12,133 --> 00:20:13,333
[GASPS]
Gasp.

384
00:20:13,467 --> 00:20:14,800
Who?

385
00:20:14,933 --> 00:20:16,133
Joey?

386
00:20:16,267 --> 00:20:18,933
Come on, Kyle, that's fake news.

387
00:20:19,167 --> 00:20:21,300
Instead of making up gossip,

388
00:20:21,433 --> 00:20:22,700
why don't you just ask him?

389
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:24,900
- Who is it really? Like that.
- Yes, that's right?

390
00:20:25,033 --> 00:20:27,500
[PHONE RINGING]

391
00:20:27,633 --> 00:20:29,000
Oh, wait.

392
00:20:31,933 --> 00:20:34,467
Hello? Yvette?

393
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,400
I'm going to the wake.

394
00:20:36,567 --> 00:20:38,767
You, when are you going?

395
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:40,133
<i> Wake?</i>

396
00:20:40,267 --> 00:20:41,533
Who died?

397
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:45,833
Clarissa's husband,
the father of your friend.

398
00:20:45,967 --> 00:20:47,700
<i>Didn't Joey tell you?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

399
00:20:47,833 --> 00:20:50,767
[STAMMERS]
No, he's not...

400
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:52,033
<i> What did you say?</i>

401
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:54,033
<i> Anyway, if you don't know,</i>

402
00:20:54,167 --> 00:20:56,933
I'll just text you
the details, okay?

403
00:20:57,067 --> 00:20:58,133
I'm in a hurry.

404
00:20:58,267 --> 00:21:00,600
I still have to pick up
what I'll bring to the wake.

405
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:02,833
Yes, you're right.

406
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:04,967
Okay, Yvette.

407
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:06,633
Thank you for letting me know.

408
00:21:07,033 --> 00:21:08,133
Take care.

409
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:09,267
Okay, okay, bye.

410
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,700
Thanks!

411
00:21:12,767 --> 00:21:14,900
[EXHALES]
Fake news.

412
00:21:15,033 --> 00:21:16,467
Hon.

413
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:18,133
Oh, Hon?

414
00:21:18,267 --> 00:21:19,833
Did I hear it right?

415
00:21:19,967 --> 00:21:21,833
You're going to Delgado's wake?

416
00:21:21,967 --> 00:21:23,167
Yes, Hon.

417
00:21:23,933 --> 00:21:24,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

418
00:21:25,067 --> 00:21:26,633
I'll go with you.

419
00:21:26,767 --> 00:21:28,500
Okay, that's good.

420
00:21:28,633 --> 00:21:30,233
I'm so happy
that you're coming with me.

421
00:21:30,367 --> 00:21:31,733
Of course.

422
00:21:31,867 --> 00:21:33,500
I also want to offer
condolences,

423
00:21:33,633 --> 00:21:36,433
and I want to make sure
that everything is in order.

424
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:38,033
Okay then, Hon,
get dressed first.

425
00:21:38,167 --> 00:21:40,300
- Okay.
- Okay, I'll just talk to nanny.

426
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,600
Nanny! Clara!

427
00:21:43,733 --> 00:21:48,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

428
00:21:58,833 --> 00:22:02,867
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

429
00:22:05,267 --> 00:22:06,867
I really have somewhere to go.

430
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,200
If it's okay, stay with mommy.

431
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:11,933
Just tell me if something
happens to mommy.

432
00:22:12,067 --> 00:22:12,800
I'll come back right away.

433
00:22:12,933 --> 00:22:13,967
Of course, yes.

434
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:15,867
You know we need to do this,

435
00:22:16,033 --> 00:22:18,267
so no one will ask
about dad anymore.

436
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:19,700
Condolence.

437
00:22:19,833 --> 00:22:21,200
Thank you, Ma'am.

438
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:22,433
Why is it closed?

439
00:22:22,567 --> 00:22:24,867
My daughter
and I can't bear to see

440
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,400
what happened to him.

441
00:22:26,533 --> 00:22:27,933
Jin Ho is the enemy.

442
00:22:28,067 --> 00:22:28,900
I knew it.

443
00:22:29,033 --> 00:22:30,200
There's really something
about that man.

444
00:22:30,333 --> 00:22:31,267
Jin Ho?

445
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:32,367
This seems old.

446
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,067
Did you get this
from the teddy bear?

447
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,667
Yes, Kisses found it.

448
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,033
Hopefully, it works.
